press/: the total experience, four ways, over one engine — and D18

The demo shelf proves capabilities one at a time. This composes them into the thing they were for: **one
page that feels like one place, while every view under it is a frame onto another origin in the subdomain
world.** Four skins over one engine, so the same machinery can be stood in four ways and compared by feel.
No new mechanism and no new cryptography — `press/` is an arrangement of `composer/`, `git-enough/`,
`jekyll-enough/` and the probe line.

    node scripts/serve-constellation.mjs   →   http://anecdote.localhost:8137/press/

## Two gestures and a verb

- **go** — a place shown *on ice* (source fetched, its face resolved, read in a sterile `data:` chamber) or
  *live* (the origin itself, framed).
- **write** — a statement with an object attached, signed here, printed into a pile here as a commit. Said
  over a page, it carries a receipt for the **version** it was said over: by hash, copying none of it.
- **read** — a floor **on another origin** holds the lens; the press does the catching, heals around damage,
  verifies, opens what arrived sterile, and writes nothing until *slap it down*.

## The face of a bottle

`index.md` wins → `README.md` shown as the index (with `library/EXHIBIT.md`'s canon as buttons and strip as
tabs) → unbuilt Jekyll rendered from source → *live* when only a built page answers → *none*, which says
"did not answer" differently from "nothing here yet".

The tree is lazy, and **the renderer is what asks for it**: `buildSite`'s lenient build names what it lacks,
each round fetches exactly that, and whatever is still missing is printed at the foot of the face. Verified
against the real thawed group — `library`'s README yields its 9-tab strip; Tell and Atlas render from their
unbuilt `index.md` + layouts with zero gaps; `journal`, which has no README at all, honestly says so.

## D18 — the library is the wildcard host; bottles is a driver

Recorded from the operator's ruling of 2026-09-19. It supersedes D4/D10/D11 on **one point only** — where a
bottle is served from — and is the record `library/OPEN.md` §1 said was owed here. It lists what it forces
(`bottle-uri.mjs`'s `BOTTLES`, the `models/` CSP, the missing SAN line) and **fixes none of it**; it names
"who owns the player" as still open and says what arrangement the press took in the meantime.

## Also: the certificate half of the library's floor

`config/san-list.txt` gains `*.library.anecdote.channel`, **as its own commit** so it can be dropped or
timed separately — merging it changes the real ACM pack via `acm-sync`. `docs/flooring.md` gains "Laying one
on Cloudflare": the operator confirmed no floor has ever actually been served, at `*.tell` or anywhere; the
certificate and the serving are independent halves; and two sources disagree on whether a Pages project
takes a wildcard custom domain under ACM — so it records the one-minute test that settles it, and the
assets-only-Worker fallback if it fails.

## The four skins

`halt` (single attention: arrive at nothing; one line is the whole interface) · `bench` (bed · sheet · rack)
· `counter` (two people present: hand over / take) · `overlay` (the *posting-from-a-phone* petition,
verbatim: a button that drops into posting mode over whatever is already rendering).

## The broadcast target, and `docs/preview-paradigm.md`

Added at the operator's request before a reboot, to make research about The Counter sturdier: **a page that
does nothing but broadcast**, and the three ways to cut a bottle up that she named — *still* (one code, one
glance), *collage* (n at once, redundancy in space), *stream* (endless, redundancy in time) — plus a second
axis for what a piece IS: *droplets* (any subset) or *blocks* (each once). Every plan reports the **floor**
of screen-reads a perfect camera would need, so the one number two phones actually produce has something to
be measured against.

`docs/preview-paradigm.md` writes down the UI observation it came from (iOS Preview/Runestone's half-screen
file browser; what a trivialized Expo app of that shape would feel like with the bottle engine in the other
half) and why The Counter is congruent with it — *"not the winner design"* but *"obviously a complete version
of the concept"*. Explicitly a shaping note: the app is ideation, the instrument is built.

**It already found things.** A block cut with no loss is *exactly* its floor — zero overhead, better than the
fountain's ~1.18× — and the fountain wins only once anything goes wrong. Nine tiles divide the floor by nine
at the same code size per tile. The still's ceiling is 2,953 frame bytes at level L, so a ~1 KB anecdote
hands over in a single glance with no video at all, which is a product fact rather than a format detail.

## Touched outside `press/`

- `composer/authorize.mjs` — two Rung-0, non-persisting ops graded: `press.follow`, `bottle.catch`.
- `composer/bottle-embed.mjs` — `embedBottle` gains `allow` (a camera must be delegated *before* the frame
  loads), `expectOrigin` (the READY's browser-attested origin is checked before the port is handed over —
  it was checked against nothing), and `title`. Additive; neither file is mirrored into another repo.
- `sw.js` — **VERSION v7 → v9**; the press, its *eager* import closure, and the broadcast target join
  `FALLBACK_SHELL` (79 paths), digests pinned in `scripts/sw.test.mjs`. The reducer's lazy naming modules
  are deliberately left out. The target is in the shell because two phones in a field with no network is
  precisely when it has to boot.
- `press/press.mjs`'s `drawFrame` takes an `ecLevel` — it hardcoded `"M"`, so the target's knob did nothing.
- `scripts/serve-constellation.mjs` — the multi-origin dev server; `scripts/test.mjs` lists `press`.

## Stand-ins, said plainly

`press/floor/` is **not** the library's floor. The signing key is minted per session; the real press asks the
keeper behind a passkey. Foreign Liquid is rendered — no I/O, no network in the chamber, so the hazard is
time, not reach — and that wants a second opinion before this is anything but a demo.

## New conduct

None. Nothing is transmitted anywhere, nothing is kept without an explicit act, and the CONSTITUTION is
untouched. Composition of attested conduct, not new conduct.

## Tests

`129/129` suites. Eight new Node suites in `press/`, one in `scripts/`, and
`probe-test/press.ui.test.mjs`: 36 checks in real Chromium on the true hostnames — arriving at the halt
fetches from no other origin; the chamber cannot reach the network and a bottle's own `<script>` does not
run in it; a link out of the constellation is announced and moves nothing; a bottle is caught **across
origins through deliberately damaged frames**; looking writes nothing; one remembered view, no trail; no
request escaped the constellation in the whole run.

## Found on the way, not fixed

- `jekyll-enough`'s fence regex does not accept an **empty** front matter (`---\n---`), which real Jekyll
  does. `press/face.mjs` deliberately uses the same fence so the two never disagree.
- `markdown-enough`'s `*emphasis*` misses when a `**bold**` run precedes it on the line.
- This `.pr` slot still held #239's draft, a merged PR. It is a slot and not an archive.

